  "source_mass_model": "R7 moving links retain the source uniform full-solid PLA mass, 55 g servos and aluminium horn geometry. Printed infill, density, fasteners and wiring on moving links are unmeasured.",
  "added_mass_model": "Hub uses the main_hub_20260915 solid volume at the repository PLA density, not measured printed mass. Battery 174 g and phone 155 g follow MIST_AVAILABLE_PARTS.md. Electronics/harness 540 g is the midpoint of the July 480 to 600 g allowance; its location is unmeasured. Phone frame/straps 55 g is an estimate; pan servo 55 g and horn 6 g follow the R5 phone CAD contract. The frame, servo and horn remain fitted when the phone is absent. Replace these masses and centres with scale and balance measurements.",
  "assembly_scope": "The hub source references print_dfm_20260914 legs. This simulation uses the R7 URDF, whose later DFM changes are not incorporated in that URDF. Joint lengths and hub mounting frames match the source CAD contracts; final manufactured parts, fasteners, cables and inter-leg clearance still need checking.",
  "phone_pose": "R5 phone.py places an upright landscape phone with its screen toward +X and long edge along Y. PAN_Z is 98 mm and PHONE_BOTTOM is 18 mm above that pan origin. The source envelope centre is therefore [3.725, 0, 151.25] mm. Pan is locked for walking. The R5 phone mounting assembly is unvalidated on the revised main hub; servo/cradle proxies here are payload assumptions, not a manufacturing assembly.",
  "collision_scope": "Primitive boxes approximate each rigid link. Only the spherical toe is intended to touch the ground. CAD meshes are used for visuals; the collisions do not prove mechanical clearance or stress.",
  "actuator_scope": "No measured continuous torque or internal controller response supplied. The 0.588 Nm initial limit is an analysis choice; it is 60 percent of the recorded 0.981 Nm rated torque.",
  "test_leg_loading": "single_leg.urdf requires useFixedBase=True; quadruped.urdf requires useFixedBase=False. Both use SI units."
}
